WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 09 · Course 4 · Protect · For entrepreneurs
Financial Management

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Set up money management from the start: roles, budgets, cash, controls and reports that earn trust.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.985
This module helps you set up money management from the start: clear finance roles, an organisational budget, a funds register, a cash forecast, controls before the first payment and simple reports. It answers: can we pay our way, and show it?

4
00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:31.985
Why money needs structure early

5
00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:38.400
1. Cash, not profit on paper, pays the bills; a forecast shows gaps early.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:45.185
2. Controls are easiest to set up before the first payment, not after a problem.

7
00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:51.489
3. Clear records earn the trust of funders, customers and co-founders.

8
00:00:51.889 --> 00:01:02.039
What you will work through: 9.1 Finance roles and the finance cycle · 9.2 The organisational budget · 9.3 Project budgets, cost allocation and full cost recovery · 9.4 Restricted and unrestricted funds · 9.5 Cash flow, forecasting and runway · 9.6 Financial controls, approvals and procurement · 9.7 Management accounts and budget versus actual · 9.8 Financial reporting: board, funders and statutory · 9.9 Audit, examination and financial governance · 9.10 Financial health and sustainability · 9.11 Recap: Financial Management

9
00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:03.039
What you will have

10
00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:07.972
1. A first-year budget that includes founder pay and reserves.

11
00:01:07.972 --> 00:01:13.646
2. A funds register, a monthly cash forecast and basic financial controls.

12
00:01:13.646 --> 00:01:19.580
3. A reporting calendar and simple measures of financial health.

13
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:20.580
Practical tips

14
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:25.143
1. Record every transaction from day one, however small.

15
00:01:25.143 --> 00:01:30.817
2. Ask someone with accounting experience to review your budget and controls.

16
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:37.491
3. Use our example bakery’s year-one figures to check your own assumptions.

17
00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:40.091
You create: Your Financial Management Pack: first-year budget, funds register, cash forecast, controls and reporting calendar.

18
00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:44.891
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:46.391 --> 00:01:49.491
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
